# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw measurement data is NOT tracked.
#
# It is regenerated by the collection harnesses (evaluation/*/collect*.sh) from
# tracked configs, so git holds what produced a number rather than the number's
# raw inputs: source, harnesses, analyzers, generators, configs, figures, and
# the per-collection logs under collect_logs/ that record what ran, its return
# code, timings and span counts.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE STARTS WITH **/ ON PURPOSE. A gitignore pattern containing
# a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so `results/**/*.csv` matches
# only a top-level results/ and silently ignores nothing else. That exact
# mistake -- as `evaluation/results/*.csv`, which also does not recurse -- is
# how 5594 files and 94 MB came to be tracked without anyone deciding to.
**/results/**/*.csv
**/results/**/*.jsonl
**/results/*.csv
**/results/*.jsonl
**/results_*.csv
**/analysis/**/*.csv

# Superseded collections, kept on disk rather than deleted but never tracked.
**/_archive*/

# MLflow tracking stores, local or otherwise. The overhead experiments record
# to a local store by design (see collect_e1.sh).
mlruns/
**/mlruns_*.db
mlflow.db
**/*.db

# Collection sentinels: recreated by the next run, meaningless in history.
**/DONE_*

# Scratch working area: throwaway probes, ablation builds, and cloned upstream
# repos (kits19, mlperf-inference) that must not become embedded submodules.
scratchpad/

# Model weights and checkpoints. Large binaries fetched or trained, not source.
models/
**/*.ptc
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.safetensors

# MLPerf run logs: multi-MB traces regenerated by every compliance run.
**/mlperf_log_*.json
**/mlperf_log_*.txt


